Usage:
  feov-record [flags]
  feov-record [command]

Available Commands:
  cite            cite a source at a quoted sentence — the tool fetches, caches, and splices an invisible immortal anchor; you never type a footnote: --quote "<the exact sentence, verbatim from the report>" --url <u> --title <t> [--key <your C1>]
  claim-index     locate every site of each FOOTNOTED claim in your report (read-only)
  closing         a ### BLUE CLOSING entry per docketed gap: --id <gap> --reason <prose>
  completion      Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  count-claims    count the FOOTNOTED declarative claims in blue's report (read-only)
  edit            replace an exact span in blue/report.md, preserving red's finding-markers: --key <your F1> --quote "<exact current span>" --new "<replacement>" --reason "..."
  fetch           cached, hash-verified web read (replaces WebFetch); serves both sides the same bytes
  friction        a capability gap or protocol misfit, as an event that survives aborts: --reason. CLOSE THIS CHANNEL EVERY SITTING: --none --reason "<what you reached for and found>" says nothing blocked you, which silence cannot say — an empty friction log reads the same whether the sitting was clean or the channel went unused
  help            Help about any command
  line-of-inquiry a direction the report could take, and what became of it — `propose` one, `move` one you already proposed
  manifest-row    one correctness-manifest receipt per repaired gap: --id R2-3 --row "figures recomputed; acceptance check run: pass; sites swept: S2,S4"
  motion          file and rule on a motion — a grade dispute, a petition, or a ruling on a direction. One mechanism, one id.
  position        the round's ### BLUE section (prose via --reason)
  prove           settle a claim by COMPUTING it: --quote "<the exact sentence>" --script <path under the run dir> [--cites <the method's citation label>] — the tool runs it twice, caches the script and its output, and splices an invisible proof anchor at that sentence
  register        FIRST ACTION at the seat: `register`, no flags of its own — just your --run and --seat-id, and a value that disagrees with the run you were dispatched into is refused rather than obeyed
  retire          remove a claim from the report, on the record: --quote "<the claim, quoted from the report as it stood>" --reason "..." [--new "<the claim that replaces it>"]
  revision        the round record itself (--reason carries what changed this round) — singleton per seat-round; emit AFTER your report edits land
  show            read a projection on STDOUT (the tool is the read path; the .md files are for human verification). With no projection named, you get YOUR PENDING WORK: report | board | findings | work | motions | debate | changes | evidence | lines-of-inquiry | telemetry

Flags:
  -h, --help             help for feov-record
      --json             emit a structured JSON result (and structured errors) instead of human text
      --run string       the run directory. REQUIRED on every call: the dispatch prompt names it. A value that DISAGREES with the run you were dispatched into is refused rather than obeyed
      --seat-id string   your seat id, as the dispatch prompt states it (SEAT_ID). REQUIRED on every call, and it SELECTS this surface: the verbs listed are the ones your seat may run
  -v, --version          version for feov-record

Use "feov-record [command] --help" for more information about a command.

